Keeps the bootable-Pi-image tooling working — configure-sd-card.sh writes and self-provisions a Pi OS card so a new Pi comes up ready.

Bootable-Pi-image creation via the `Berrylands/cloud-init-init` repo: `configure-sd-card.sh` writes a Raspberry Pi OS image to an SD card and provisions it (WiFi, SSH keys, AWS creds, cloud-init user-data) so the Pi self-provisions on first boot. Spans `Berrylands/cloud-init-init` (the tooling) and the fleet hosts it images.
